M03_Chinook_ParaDrop::Created formatted its owner's object id into
char params[10] with sprintf before handing it to M03_Reinforcement_Chinook.
In retail M03 the owner is always an "Invisible_Object" created at runtime by
M03_Beach_Reinforce (Reinforce_Beach/Inlet/Base) or
M03_Inlet_Nod_Reinforcements, so its id is a dynamic id (>= 1500000000, ten
digits). Ten digits plus the terminator need 11 bytes, so every paradrop wrote
one byte past the stack buffer. Enlarge it to 16 bytes and bound the write
with snprintf. The formatted text is unchanged for every id.

--- a/Mission03.cpp
+++ b/Mission03.cpp
@@ -4709,8 +4709,8 @@
 
 		dead = false;
 		out = 0;
-		char params[10];
-		sprintf(params, "%d", Commands->Get_ID(obj));
+		char params[16];
+		snprintf(params, sizeof(params), "%d", Commands->Get_ID(obj));
 		Commands->Attach_Script(chinook, "M03_Reinforcement_Chinook", params);
 
 		chinook_id = Commands->Get_ID(chinook);
